# Modules the initramfs needs, in dependency order. There are none.
#
# This file exists to say that deliberately. modules-initfs.downstream is a
# hundred lines long because the stock 5.10 tree builds its whole SoC support
# as loadable modules and the initramfs has to name every one in probe order.
# Our mainline config does the opposite: the clock controller, pinctrl, the
# SPMI arbiter, the RPMh regulators, the SMMU, sdhci-msm, the GENI serial
# console, dwc3 and the HS PHY are all CONFIG_*=y, so they are in vmlinux and
# have probed before the initramfs runs at all.
#
# The USB gadget functions are modules (CONFIG_USB_CONFIGFS=m), but
# postmarketos-initramfs already lists usb_f_acm, usb_f_ncm, usb_f_rndis and
# usb_f_mass_storage in its own 00-default.modules, and mkinitfs follows
# modinfo dependencies from there, so libcomposite, u_ether and u_serial come
# along without being named. ext4 and the crypto it needs are on that list
# too.
#
# If something here ever stops being builtin, it belongs in this file rather
# than in the config.
